  "description": "This isn't a bike you can tour, this is a Touring Bike.\n\nIf you believe in using only the best tools and the job is long-distance touring,\n\nthis is your bike.\n\nFuji Touring's long-wheelbase double-butted Cro-moly frame is relaxed in its\n\nangles for stability in loaded touring mode. It comes with a rear rack and\n\nis equipped to take a front rack or Low Rider pannier mount. It has cantilever\n\nbrake bosses, two bottle cage mounts and a spare spoke holder on one chain\n\nstay.\n\nShimano provides sealed cartridge bottom bracket. And the Sora STI Mega-Range\n\ntouring gears: three chain rings, nine cogs. Shimano also supplies the hubs, strung by 36, 14-gauge, stainless spokes to double\n\nwall aluminum rims carrying fat Ritchey tires. Brakes are Avid cantis, the\n\nalloy headset a roller-bearing model from Full Speed Ahead.\n\nYou can ride this bike to work or to run errands. You could ride it on your\n\nclub's weekend outings. Shame to waste it, though. Planning to pedal across\n\nSiberia? Perfect. Fuji Touring.",
